   "id": "5e0b8366-4f41-4b5c-8e9e-5128682459ad",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "__SIMPLE LINEAR REGRESSION:-\n",
    " regression - is supervised learning algorithm, which has continuous values or numerical values.\n",
    "- it is the most commonly used predicting analysis.\n",
    "- it explains the relationship between independent variable and dependent variable using straight line.\n",
    "- the straight line is plotted on scatter plot\n",
    "- it is called as simple linear regression because the independent feature  will only be one as well as dependent featue will also be only one and they both should form a realtionship amongst each other.\n",
    "- equation: Y=B0 + B1X\n",
    "        where, B0 is the intercept/error point and B1X is the slope of the graph.\n",
    "- the predicting line would never over ride.\n",
    "- machine learning will never give 100% accuracy the most closest value will be the best approach.\n",
    "- the prediction line is called as best fit line.\n",
    "- the best fit line is found by minimising the expression of RSS (residual sum of squares).\n",
    "- Error is claculated using , error = square of (actual - predicted ) +.....=sse"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "569cb098-ab46-406d-9e26-8c924f42e13f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "__NOTE:-\n",
    "- the input features are independent in nature that means it should not depend on each other.\n",
    "- we will check the independency of the input feature by using correlation.\n",
    "- target feature which is represented by y is dependent on input feature .\n",
    "- linear regression works only with this kind of data where target feature is depended on input feature.\n",
    "- when the scatter plot graph some what forms a straight line then we can say that linear regression can be applied on that data set.\n"
   ]
  },
